{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1131","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1131","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1131\",\"parent_revision\":\"e8c1c0fb23026a497e03944f89f76d1677d1ad6a8e37a5a4890a5002b727ece2\",\"root_revision\":\"e8c1c0fb23026a497e03944f89f76d1677d1ad6a8e37a5a4890a5002b727ece2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPhase 1 of #282 flipped the write path to GH-first but the read path and artifact registration were not addressed. Three gaps remain:\\n\\n1. discovery/SKILL.md and planning/SKILL.md write .planning/harness/DISCOVERY.md and .planning/harness/PLAN.md to disk with no backlog_update call \u2014 these artifacts are invisible to the backend and any other session/machine.\\n\\n2. work-backlog-item/SKILL.md line 138 reads detailed fields (description, source, research_first, suggested_location) directly from file_path on disk. If the local cache does not exist (fresh clone, different machine), this step fails.\\n\\n3. create-backlog-item/SKILL.md line 165 scans ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/ on disk for duplicate detection instead of querying the MCP backend (backlog_list with title filter).\\n\\nThe backend is used for all writes but reads still fall back to local disk files, and discovery/plan artifacts are never registered with the backend.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: skills still assume local disk cache for reads and don't register discovery/plan artifacts in backend** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 identified during groom of #282 (GH-first backlog redesign Phase 1)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-30\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"db99f8cd56dd2be36f5bf299c169402ceee10cc3a15a7a394962e07ae09d9bd6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWSbHQ\"}"}